  "body": "## Problem\npkgs/fleet/crates/fleet-queue/src/validate.rs on current main does not compile under the queue-broker feature: error[E0308] at validate.rs:16 — pub const FLEET_REPOS: [&str; 10] declares 10 but lists 9 repos (code, opencode, openchamber, forks/opencode, forks/openchamber, dezren39/nix, dezren39/darwin-nix, zettel, dezren39/dezren39). Verified identical on clean origin/main during task 13349 (PR #7061 shepherd, 2026-11-08); PR #7061 does not touch this file.\n\n## Impact\ncargo test -p fleet-queue --features queue-broker (and any queue-broker build) fails on main. Default-feature builds are unaffected, which is likely why it slipped through.\n\n## Fix options\nChange the declared size to 9, or add the missing 10th repo if one was intended (the rename comment above the constant suggests old+new names were being counted).\n\n## Acceptance\n- cargo test -p fleet-queue --features queue-broker compiles and passes on main.\n- The intended list size (9 vs 10) is confirmed in the fixing PR.\n\nFound by: queue worker lane code-f, task 13349, 2026-11-08.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `cargo test -p fleet-queue --features queue-broker` compiles and passes on main (CI or laptop per fleet policy — no sandbox builds).\n- The fixing PR states the intended repo list size explicitly (9 as listed, or the missing 10th repo named and added) — the declared array size and the list agree.\n- A default-feature build is unaffected.\n",
